.TH BACAK-COMPOSITOR 1 "June 2026" "BDM 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bacak-compositor \- prototype weston-backed compositor for the BDM greeter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bacak-compositor
.RB [ --greeter
.IR PATH ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bacak-compositor
is a prototype stand-in for the (not-yet-written) native Bacak compositor. It
wraps
.BR weston (1),
generating a configuration that uses the kiosk shell and weston's
.B [autolaunch]
to host the greeter given by
.B --greeter
fullscreen. With
.B watch=true
weston exits when the greeter exits, letting
.BR bacak-display-manager (8)
proceed to the user session.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WESTON_BACKEND
Force a weston backend module (e.g.
.IR x11-backend.so ,
.IR wayland-backend.so ,
.IR headless-backend.so ).
On real hardware, leave unset so weston auto-selects the drm backend.
.TP
.B WESTON_EXTRA_ARGS
Extra arguments passed to weston (e.g.
.IR "--width=1024 --height=720" ).
.TP
.B BDM_WESTON_CONFIG
Path to a base weston config to extend (kiosk shell + greeter autolaunch are
always appended).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/bacak-display-manager/weston-greeter.ini
Reference weston configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bacak-display-manager (8),
.BR bacak-greeter (1),
.BR weston (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Bacak Desktop Project.
